---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";

const effective = "September 10, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms that govern your use of ${SITE.name}, including content ownership and pattern copyright.`}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated {effective}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with
        them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the content</h2>
      <p>
        Everything written here is free to read, and you are welcome to make
        anything you learn from it, including items you sell. You do not owe me a
        credit or a fee for a finished object.
      </p>
      <p>What you may not do is republish the material itself:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Do not copy an article, a chart, or a tutorial onto another website,
          in whole or in substantial part, in any language.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not distribute the charts as your own PDF, printable, or paid
          product.
        </li>
        <li>
          You may quote a short passage or one row of a chart with a visible
          credit and a working link back to the page it came from.
        </li>
        <li>
          You may link to any page here freely, including in your own patterns
          and video descriptions. That is encouraged.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Pattern copyright</h2>
      <p>
        The free pattern round-ups on this site link to patterns owned by the
        designers who wrote them. Those patterns are not mine and are not covered
        by anything above. Their terms are set by their authors on their own
        pages, and you should read them, particularly if you intend to sell what
        you make.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a designer and you would like your work removed from a
        round-up, or the credit or photo changed, email me and it will be handled
        promptly. No explanation required.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy, and the limits of it</h2>
      <p>
        The charts and tutorials here are researched carefully and corrected when
        readers find problems, but they are provided as-is with no warranty. Yarn
        behaves differently between brands and dye lots, hands work at different
        tensions, and manufacturers change their sizing. Always check your own
        gauge before committing to a large project.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here is professional advice of any kind. To the extent permitted
        by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any loss arising from your use of
        the site, including wasted yarn, a garment that came out the wrong size,
        or a project that did not work.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        This site carries advertising and affiliate links, described on the
        <a href="/disclosures">disclosures page</a>. Advertisements are served by
        third parties and their presence is not an endorsement by me.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided without any guarantee of uptime. Pages may be
        changed, corrected, or removed at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated. The date at the top will change when they
        are, and continuing to use the site means you accept the revised version.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
